⭐ 2. How to Wear It
The hat must sit:

Level on your head

Snug enough that it moves with your head

With the tiny OLED screen facing forward

With the vibration motors positioned:

Front = forehead

Back = rear band

Left = left temple

Right = right temple

This ensures accurate directional alerts.

⭐ 3. How the Hat Connects to Your Phone
Your phone is the brain.
The hat is the body.

Your phone sends:

Compass heading

Navigation instructions

Object detection (cars, bikes, people, animals)

Speed + direction of approach

Weather

Danger flag

The hat receives this over Wi‑Fi and reacts instantly.

⭐ 4. Head‑Gesture Controls (The Go Time Gesture OS)
The hat is controlled entirely by head movements.

🎯 Nod = Select / Confirm
A clean downward nod selects the highlighted mode or confirms an action.

🎯 Tilt Right = Next
Tilt your head to the right to move forward through modes.

🎯 Tilt Left = Previous
Tilt your head to the left to move backward through modes.

🎯 Shake = Back / Exit
A quick “no” shake returns you to Awareness Mode.

These gestures work while walking, skating, or standing still.

⭐ 5. The Modes (Gesture‑Navigated)
You cycle through modes by tilting left/right.
You enter a mode by nodding.
You exit a mode by shaking.

🟡 Mode 1 — Awareness Mode (Default)
This is the hat’s main operating mode.

Screen shows:

Big direction letter (N, NE, E…)

Object alerts

Speed class

Direction of approach

Hat vibrates based on:

Direction

Speed

Sensitivity mode

This is your always‑on safety mode.

🧭 Mode 2 — Compass Mode
Screen shows:

Heading number (0–360°)

Big direction letter

Rotating arrow

Gestures:

Tilt Right → Switch display style

Tilt Left → Switch display style

Nod → Lock heading

Shake → Back to Awareness

🧭➡️ Mode 3 — Navigation Mode
Your phone sends turn‑by‑turn instructions.

Screen shows:

“TURN LEFT IN 200 FT”

“TURN RIGHT NOW”

“CONTINUE STRAIGHT”

Hat vibrates in the direction of the turn.

Gestures:

Nod → Confirm next step

Tilt Right → Skip

Tilt Left → Repeat

Shake → Back

🕶️ Mode 4 — Stealth Mode
Screen goes minimal.
Only haptics are active.

Perfect for night walks or when you want silent awareness.

⚙️ Mode 5 — System Mode
Screen shows:

Brightness

Vibration strength

Radar sensitivity

Phone link status

Safety Sensitivity Mode (Crowd / Balanced / Home‑Alone)

Tilt Left/Right to change settings.
Nod to confirm.

🌦️ Mode 6 — Weather Mode
Screen shows:

Temperature

Weather summary

Wind speed

Data comes from your phone.

⭐ 6. Safety Sensitivity Levels (Go Time Safety Profiles)
These determine how reactive the hat is.

🟢 Crowd Mode (Low Sensitivity)
Use in:

Festivals

Beltline

Stores

Busy sidewalks

Alerts ONLY when:

Someone approaches fast

Someone approaches directly from behind

A bike or runner is overtaking you

A car is approaching

No alerts for slow walkers.

🟡 Balanced Mode (Normal Sensitivity)
Use for everyday walking.

Alerts when:

Someone is closing distance

Someone approaches from behind

Bikes, runners, cars

Medium or fast movement

This is the default.

🔴 Home‑Alone Mode (Maximum Sensitivity)
Use when:

Walking home alone

Parking lots

Empty streets

Trails

Late at night

Alerts on ANY approach:

Slow

Medium

Fast

Any direction

Any object

This is full Go Time mode.

⭐ 7. Danger Override (“GO TIME”)
If your phone detects:

A fast‑approaching object

A threat

A dangerous trajectory

A vehicle closing too quickly

A person running directly at you

It sends:

Code
danger = 1
The hat immediately:

🔥 Vibrates ALL motors continuously
🔥 Displays “GO TIME” on the screen
🔥 Shows object + direction + speed
🔥 Ignores all other modes
🔥 Stays in GO TIME until danger clears
This is your emergency alert system.

⭐ 8. Directional Vibration Language
The hat vibrates based on direction:

Front → forehead motor

Back → rear motor

Left → left temple

Right → right temple

Diagonals → two motors at once

Speed determines intensity:

Slow → short pulse

Medium → double pulse

Fast → long pulse

Danger → continuous vibration.

⭐ 9. How to Use the Hat (Quick Start)
1. Put on the hat
Make sure it fits snug.

2. Open the Go Time phone app
It connects automatically.

3. Start walking
The hat enters Awareness Mode.

4. Switch modes
